    "BrochureContent": [
      {
        "ContentType": "Description",
        "SortOrder": 0,
        "Content": "In one of Donegal`s most sought-after coastal locations, this outstanding five-bedroom detached residence enjoys breathtaking views over Rossnowlagh Beach to the Atlantic Ocean. Combining generous family accommodation with an unrivalled setting, this impressive home offers a rare opportunity to acquire a premium property in the heart of Ireland`s renowned Wild Atlantic Way. \n\nDesigned to maximise its spectacular surroundings, the property is flooded with natural light, with spacious reception rooms and principal living areas perfectly positioned to capture the ever-changing sea views. The well-appointed kitchen and dining area provide an ideal space for both everyday family living and entertaining with adjoining patio, while the cozy living room offers a relaxing retreat.\n\nThe accommodation extends to five generously proportioned bedrooms, including a luxurious principal suite, enjoys a balcony with beautiful Atlantic sea-views. Beautifully presented throughout, the home combines comfort, quality, and timeless style.\n\nExternally, the property sits on mature landscaped grounds, offering privacy and ample outdoor space to relax and enjoy the spectacular coastal scenery. A generous driveway provides extensive parking, while the surrounding gardens create a peaceful setting just moments from the beach.\n\nRossnowlagh is celebrated for its golden sandy beach, world-class surfing, scenic coastal walks, and vibrant local community. \nThe area offers an exceptional lifestyle, with nearby restaurants, cafés, hotels, and leisure amenities, while the thriving towns of Ballyshannon and Donegal Town are within easy reach, providing an excellent range of shops, schools, and services.\n\nWhether as a distinguished family home, luxury holiday residence, or investment opportunity, this exceptional property offers an enviable combination of space, location, and uninterrupted sea views in one of the northwest`s most desirable coastal destinations."
      },
